# Google Maps browser key lives in js/config.js and IS committed on purpose.
# A Maps JavaScript key is public by design — the browser sends it to Google on
# every map load, so hiding it from git protects nothing and breaks the deploy
# (Cloudflare Pages builds from this repo). It is secured in Google Cloud Console
# by HTTP-referrer restriction + API restriction, which is Google's own guidance.
# Keys for server-side/one-off scripts (Places, Geocoding) must NOT be committed.

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Temp Word files
~$*

